.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_TO_STREAM 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_to_stream
.Nd build a stream from an iterator
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fo dtfl_to_stream
.Fa "dtfl_scope *scope"
.Fa "const dtfl_type *type"
.Fa "dtfl_iter_fn next"
.Fa "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_to_stream
creates a source operator in
.Fa scope
that replays the records produced by
.Fa next
at the minimum time.
On each schedule the operator calls
.Fa next ,
which emits a record through its
.Vt dtfl_emit
sink and returns true, until it returns false to signal the end.
A bounded number of records is produced per schedule, so a long
iterator does not block the worker; the operator reschedules itself
until the iterator is exhausted, then releases its capability so the
output frontier can advance.
The output stream carries records of
.Fa type .
.Pp
The context in
.Fa ctx
is passed to
.Fa next .
When
.Fa ctx
carries a destructor, the operator owns the context and releases it
when the operator is dropped.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_to_stream
returns the new stream, owned by the scope.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static bool range_next(void *ctx, dtfl_emit *out) {
	size_t *i = ctx;
	unsigned char buf[8];
	if (*i >= 100)
		return false;
	dtfl_put_u64(buf, (*i)++);
	dtfl_emit_record(out, buf, sizeof buf);
	return true;
}

size_t i = 0;
dtfl_stream *s = dtfl_to_stream(scope, dtfl_type_u64(), range_next,
    DTFL_CTX(&i, NULL));
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn dtfl_to_stream
does not return an error code.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_concat 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_count 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_exchange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_map 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_partition 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Fn to_stream
operator.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The operator and its stream belong to the worker thread that built
them and must not be shared.
